{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "Does Kainode offer Singapore VPS hosting?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Kainode runs a Singapore datacenter that was recently relaunched in 2026 after a prior supply-side pause. The SG VPS plans are the same VDS Pro / VDS Business / VDS Enterprise tiers as other regions, with monthly renewal at $16.99, $19.52, and $29.99 respectively."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How does Kainode pricing compare to Vultr for Singapore?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Kainode VDS Business at $19.52/mo (3 vCPU, 6 GB, 100 GB NVMe, 5 TB) sits between Vultr's $24/mo 2 vCPU/4 GB Singapore plan and RackNerd's occasional Singapore promos around $11.99/yr. For sustained mid-tier workloads Kainode is competitive, but Vultr's broader instance catalog and hourly billing win on flexibility."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Is Kainode good for AI agent workloads?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Kainode is rated 3.7/5 on VPSTier.com. The VDS plans are well-suited for light to medium AI agent workloads, container hosts, and reverse proxy nodes. For GPU-heavy or 16+ vCPU inference workloads, look at hyperscaler regions or providers with explicit GPU tiers."}}]}
